findings.recommendation:
Log conditionally based on whether OnceLock::set succeeded. Example:
  match JWT_TTL.set(value) {
    Ok(()) => tracing::info!(..., "seeded to {value}s ..."),
    Err(_) => tracing::debug!("seed_jwt_ttl_from_env called again; OnceLock already set to {}s, ignoring", jwt_ttl_secs()),
  }
Alternatively, use get_or_init with a closure so the INFO log is inside the init closure — it only fires once by construction.

Add a second logs_contain assertion after the whitespace-only call:
  assert!(logs_contain("MCP_JWT_TTL_SECS is empty / whitespace-only"));
after line 3210, to independently confirm the whitespace sub-case. Not blocking.
